# Applied to the upload of EVERY Vercel project built from this repository,
# immediately after the clone and before any Root Directory setting is resolved.
# Both the Go API project and the web app project deploy from here, so anything
# excluded is excluded for both.
#
# EVERY PATTERN MUST BE ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH. These are gitignore
# patterns: an unanchored `docs/` matches a directory named docs at ANY depth,
# so it also deleted web/content/docs/ — the entire documentation — from the
# upload, and the deployed site served 404s for every /docs page while the rest
# of the app worked. Anchor, or it will happen again to config/ or proto/.
#
# For the same reason web/ is not listed at all: excluding it removed the app
# the web project exists to build. Carrying it in the API project's upload costs
# a little transfer and nothing else.
#
# The dataset under data/ is embedded into the Go function and MUST ship.
/docs/
/proto/
/.sources/
/config/
/coverage.out
